        "original_id": "8b1f12d7-881a-5e28-808d-efdeec6ef1f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Norbert Holm, Erwin Rommel\n- Roles: general, field marshal, Chief of Operations, military theorist\n- Organizations: Wehrmacht, Nazi Germany\n- Events: World War II, 20 July plot\n\nFacts:\n- Erwin Rommel was born on 15 November 1891 and died on 14 October 1944.\n- Norbert Holm was born on 16 December 1895 and died on 3 June 1962.\n- Erwin Rommel was a German general and military theorist.\n- During World War II, Erwin Rommel served as a field marshal in the Wehrmacht of Nazi Germany and was popularly known as the Desert Fox.\n- During World War II, Norbert Holm was a general in the Wehrmacht of Nazi Germany.\n- Following the 20 July plot, Norbert Holm was arrested on 16 September 1944 and was later demoted because of his association, as Chief of Operations, with Field Marshal Erwin Rommel.",
